---
/**
 * C-5 · Expectations / response — `CONTACT_WIREFRAME.md` C-5 (Page IA Stage D).
 * Component (Inventory): **Response Expectations**.
 *
 * Responsibility realized: "remove post-submission uncertainty by stating what
 * happens next (how, and roughly when a reply comes)."
 *
 * Spatial composition, transcribed: "a short, reassuring statement near the
 * form — *'You'll hear back within [timeframe].'* **No artificial urgency, no
 * persuasion, no countdown** — only calm, honest expectation-setting."
 *
 * ── THE TIMEFRAME IS A FACT NOBODY HAS AUTHORED ────────────────────────────
 * The wireframe itself writes it as a bracketed slot, `[timeframe]`, and
 * `CONTACT_PAGE_IA.md` §"Open" lists "the stated response-time expectation (C-5
 * content)" among the page's unresolved dependencies. The Homepage ships a
 * placeholder row ("in cel mult 48h (substituent)"), but a response time on the
 * page where an enquiry is actually sent is a commitment a visitor plans
 * around — it is exactly the class of value §10.4 keeps out of production
 * output.
 *
 * So the string is PENDING (empty) and this module renders nothing. What the
 * page loses is reassurance; what it would lose by guessing is the honesty the
 * whole "calm principle" rests on. The moment C authors a timeframe, one string
 * in `lib/i18n/contact.ts` turns this module on.
 */
interface Props {
  copy: string;
}

const { copy } = Astro.props;
---

{copy && <p class="c-expectation rv" data-rv="meta">{copy}</p>}
